[{"location":"#AlgebraCore","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Bienvenido a la documentación de AlgebraCore.jl, un paquete diseñado para definir y operar con expresiones algebraicas simples, siguiendo principios idiomáticos de Julia como el múltiple despacho y la composición funcional.","category":"page"},{"location":"#Tabla-de-Contenidos","page":"Home","title":"Tabla de Contenidos","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Pages = [\"index.md\"]\nDepth = 2","category":"page"},{"location":"#Tipos","page":"Home","title":"Tipos","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.ScalarOp","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.ScalarOp","text":"ScalarOp{T}\n\nEstructura que representa un escalar algebraico tipado. Sirve como base para definir operaciones algebraicas con múltiples despacho.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"#Operaciones-Aritméticas","page":"Home","title":"Operaciones Aritméticas","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.add","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.add","text":"add(a::ScalarOp, b::ScalarOp)\n\nSuma dos objetos ScalarOp, promoviendo sus tipos antes de operar.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.sub","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.sub","text":"sub(a::ScalarOp, b::ScalarOp)\n\nResta dos objetos ScalarOp, promoviendo sus tipos antes de operar.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.mul","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.mul","text":"mul(a::ScalarOp, b::ScalarOp)\n\nMultiplica dos objetos ScalarOp, promoviendo sus tipos antes de operar.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.div_safe","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.div_safe","text":"div_safe(a::ScalarOp, b::ScalarOp)\n\nDivide dos objetos ScalarOp, promoviendo sus tipos antes de operar. Validación para evitar división por cero.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#Comparaciones","page":"Home","title":"Comparaciones","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"#Base.:==","page":"Home","title":"Base.:==","text":"==(a::ScalarOp{T1}, b::ScalarOp{T2}) where {T1, T2}\n\nComparación exacta entre dos ScalarOp. Solo compara los valores internos, no los tipos.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#Base.isapprox","page":"Home","title":"Base.isapprox","text":"isapprox(a::ScalarOp, b::ScalarOp; kwargs...)\n\nComparación aproximada entre dos ScalarOp, utilizando el valor interno value. Permite pasar tolerancias configurables.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#Base.hash","page":"Home","title":"Base.hash","text":"hash(a::ScalarOp, h::UInt)\n\nFunción hash requerida si se define ==, para uso en diccionarios y sets.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#Tolerancia-y-control-de-errores","page":"Home","title":"Tolerancia y control de errores","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.Tolerance.get_tolerance","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.Tolerance.get_tolerance","text":"get_tolerance() -> Real\n\nObtiene la tolerancia global actual para las operaciones de comparación.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.Tolerance.set_tolerance!","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.Tolerance.set_tolerance!","text":"set_tolerance!(tol::Real) -> Nothing\n\nEstablece la tolerancia global para las operaciones de comparación. El valor debe ser un número real.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#AlgebraCore.Tolerance.with_tolerance","page":"Home","title":"AlgebraCore.Tolerance.with_tolerance","text":"with_tolerance(f::Function, tol::Real) -> Any\n\nEjecuta la función f con una tolerancia temporal tol. Restablece el valor original al finalizar, incluso si ocurre un error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#Referencias","page":"Home","title":"Referencias","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Repositorio en GitHub","category":"page"}]
